====Quotations====
{{timeline|1600s=1603|1700s=1788}}
* '''1603''' - [[w:Michel de Montaigne|Michel de Montaigne]], ''Essayes'', Volumes 5-6‎, p. 3-4:
*: He was deceived; for justice hath also knowledge and '''animadversion''' over such as gather stubble (as the common saying is) or looke about for gape-seed. 
* '''1788''' — [[w:Alexander Hamilton|Alexander Hamilton]], ''The Federalist Papers'', Federalist No. 67 -- The Executive Department:
*: Nor have I scrupled, in so flagrant a case, to allow myself a '''animadversion''' little congenial with the general spirit of these papers.

